WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.469
-Our first guest tonight is the
Emmy-nominated co-head writer

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.272
of "Saturday Night Live,"
who also serves as co-anchor

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.774
of "Weekend Update,"
his latest stand up special

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.043
"Shame the Devil" is streaming
now on Netflix.

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:12.845
Please welcome back to the show,
our very good friend,

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:13.946
Michael Che, everybody.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.648
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:22.889 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:30.096 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.232
Welcome back.
-How you doin'. Hi.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:36.302
-I'm doing great.
-I never --

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.273
I never know what to do with the
mask after I take it off.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.608
-Yeah. Well I think a pocket
is the right answer.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:46.412
-Yeah?
-I think you're crushing it.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:48.815
-I got this fear that, like,
this is going gonna all

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.416
end up in the ocean
on some turtle.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.719
-Oh, yeah. Well it's very good
to think that way.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:56.255
I think that's -- I heard --
we're always happy to see you

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:58.824
but I heard you have a little
bit of a bone to pick with me.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:02.495
-Yeah, I do.
-Okay.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.829
-You took my look, man.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:07.233
I wanted to be casual
on "Late Night" first.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.403
You know, every -- every year
I've always asked Lorin

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.773
and the show, like, please,
let me just be casual.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.876
I want to wear my own clothes
at "Update."

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:21.080
And they said "No,
Seth wouldn't do that."

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.282
And now Seth.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.017
-Is casual.
-Well, you know why

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.819
I got away with it
and you didn't?

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:33.893
-No. Why.
-Lorin watches "SNL."

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.029
That's how they get you.
-Touché.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.297
-That's how they get you. Did
you know -- I have to ask --

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:40.800
this is a little in the weeds
on the job

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.036
I used to have that you have
now. Did you wear suit pants?

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:46.305
-No. No.
I don't wear any pants.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:50.209
-Yeah, yeah. I'm very bummed
that I -- you know --

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:51.978
I wore jeans all the time.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.480
-Which was fine,
presented fine.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.882
But there is a lot of like cool
back stage photos

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.951
you get over the years,
and you look super dumb.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:02.989
I wish jeans with the top suit
is so stupid.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.424
-Yeah, you look like --
what's that guy,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.792
"You Might Be a Redneck."
-Yeah. Well, it is.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.195
Like, when you think of it,
it's like the mullet of outfits.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.031
-Yeah.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.501
-Business up top.
Party on the bottom.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.804
-That was, like,
the comedian, like, uniform.

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:21.274
-Like jeans, a dumb blazer.
-Back in the day, yeah.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.509
-Yeah.
-And then high-tops.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.810
Like big, powerful, like,
red high tops.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.279
-Yeah, you gonna get you a
development deal

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:30.516
if you dress like that.
-1989 development deal.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.486
You -- congratulations,
I know you moved.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.221
You got yourself place
Upstate New York.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.123
-That's right.
I'm a home owner now.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.958
-Yeah. Congratulations.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.060
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.795
How is --
how is the neighborhood?

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.129
How are you taking to
the neighborhood.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:47.900
-Very, very white.
-Okay.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.503
-It's the whitest neighborhood
I've ever been to.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:56.709
It's like -- it's like me and
one black bear. And that's it.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.579
I can't wait to meet him, too.
-Well, yeah.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:02.582
-Excited.
-Is it a town?

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.084
-It's what they call a hamlet.
-Oh, wow.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.955
-Do you know what that is?
-It's white, I think. Yeah.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:12.925
-There is nobody like,
"Oh, I live in a black hamlet."

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.160
Othello?

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.262
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.729
That was for us.
-That was very good.

00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:21.100
There's someone with a
pipe watching right now going,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.437
"Oh, very well played, Che."
-Nicely played.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:29.108
-Nicely played. I will show this
to my class tomorrow.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.543
So you live --
what about Thanksgiving?

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.511
Are you going to do it there,
going to do it with your family?

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:36.782
-I'm going to probably go see
my mom, because I got to work.

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:38.651
I'M WORKING LIKE THIS WHOLE
Week.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.520
So I'm just going to go to my
mom's house.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.188
And I'm just gonna wait until
it's late

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.389
so it's not too crowded.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.392
Because my mom
has a huge Thanksgiving.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.861
-Was last year small
because of the pandemic.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.629
-No.
-Okay.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:52.732
-Well, see, she thought it was
small because she said

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:53.900
it would only be a few people.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.068
She was like, "We'll only have
like 10 people."

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.669
But my mother thinks
if she invites her family

00:03:57.669 --> 00:04:01.840
that counts as one person.
So I'll be like 10 people?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.110
Just, like, Derek and the kids,
so that's one.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.246
That's 11 what are you?

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.415
And in her head that's how she
does math.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:12.852
-Do you have to bring anything?
-No, but I get to take stuff.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.187
-Oh.
-Yeah, that's the tradition.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.223
Is when you --
you know, Thanksgiving,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:22.795
you get to take a pie home
if you've been on TV.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.363
If I was --
I wish I was on a hit show.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.366
If I was on "Squid Game" I'd
probably get a whole turkey leg.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.869
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:33.439
-What about -- you had -- I
guess what are you like eight,

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.174
nine episode into the season?
-Yeah.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.643
-Do you have anything --
I always like to ask --

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.312
anything you wrote
that you liked

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.346
that was like a complete
non-starter?

00:04:41.346 --> 00:04:43.449
-Oh, man, I don't know if it
was a non-starter.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:47.487
But it didn't go anywhere.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.355
Some things are just fun for me.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.291
Like I had this sketch --
I wrote a sketch about a guy --

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:56.061
it was a about a guy who was
have a wet coma.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:05:00.499
-A wet coma?
-Yeah.

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:03.069
It was like a wet dream,
but a coma.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.671
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:09.308
-Just so we can all --

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:11.244
I think everybody is trying to
picture that right now.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:14.247
We might as well put the host to
it. Who did you write it for?

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.414
-Owen Wilson.
-Okay.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:19.184
So Owen Wilson --
and so he is in a coma.

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:22.688
So who -- who recognized he was
having a wet coma.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:24.356
-The doctor.

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.292
Because his kids
come to visit him,

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.728
and he is just moaning
the whole time.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:35.667
Like, "Ohh."
"Mmm." "Oohh."

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:39.639
And apparently
you can't put that on NBC.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.940
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.909
-I have a lot of questions
about your special.

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.745
We'll be right back with more
from Michael Che.

